{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He called their name Adam.</b> According to Adam's own preference He called it. As found in the Tanḥuma and in Shoḥar Tov: HaShem said to him, 'You — what is your name?' He said to Him, 'It seems to me that I should be called Adam, for I was created from the earth (adamah).' 'And I — what is My name?' He said to Him, 'It is fitting for you to be called YHWH, for You are lord of all the world.' And so it says, 'אני ה׳ הוא שמי' — that is My name, which the first Adam called Me. This passage is repeated for the sake of the naming."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The paraphrase adapts a midrashic exchange (found in Tanḥuma and Shoḥar Tov) in which Adam names both himself and God; 'ה״‎שקרא' rendered as 'the name which he called Me.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:06.725882263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}